  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile models outperform image-only models, and the best completed configuration is config_005: scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool with validation accuracy 0.650 and F1 0.628. For PCA multiprofile, avgpool outperformed transformer, but that comparison has not yet been made for the best encoder, scvi_n200. config_006 changes only the aggregation method from avgpool to transformer while keeping the same RNA encoder and multiprofile setting, directly testing whether transformer aggregation can improve on the current best RNA representation. This is the best next experiment because it is a controlled extension of the most promising direction, may identify a higher-performing configuration, and clarifies whether aggregation choice matters for the strongest RNA encoder before spending budget on more complex multimodal fusion."
}

